  "_about": "a European badger SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-06, gen: scratchpad sc/must/badger.py): 75 cm nose to rump and a short 15 cm tail, low and wedge-shaped, broadest and highest at the hips, on short thick black legs; long pale digging claws on the forefeet; a small tapering head ending in a pig-like nose pad, small white-tipped ears set low and far back. The face white with two sharp black stripes from beside the nose over the eyes and ears to the neck, the throat black; the body coarse grizzled grey; legs and underside black -- painted per pixel (the `badger` pattern, coatpat.js badgerOf) in the rest pose's own space SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw, hclaw (10 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), white edged; the roots faired. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 9 dark brown whiskers a side, 3 rows on the whisker pad (30-45 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh).",
